        ]
      },
      "worked": "By the total probability rule and independence,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=P(A\\mid B)P(B)+P(A\\mid\\overline{B})P(\\overline{B})\\\\P(A)&=P(A)P(B)+0.5(1-P(B))\\\\P(A)(1-P(B))&=0.5(1-P(B)).\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe given conditional probability requires $P(\\overline{B})>0$, so cancel $1-P(B)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(A)&=0.5\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=P(A)P(B)\\\\P(A\\cap B)&=0.5P(B)\\\\0.2&=0.5P(B)\\\\P(B)&=0.4.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
